So the 100,000,000th self number is indeed 1,022,727,208.

is_self agrees with the sieve below 10,000: true
n = 2^24036583 - 1 = 299410429404...882733969407 has 7,235,733 digits.
A generator g = n - k needs digitsum(g) = k with k <= 9 * 7235733 = 65,121,597, and taking
that from n changes only its last 9 digits (733969407): digitsum(g) = 32,580,385 + digitsum(733969407 - k).
So k is from 32,580,385 to 32,580,466, and none of those fits:
2^24036583 - 1 is a self number: true
